Perform a performance-focused review of this Next.js App Router page. The team has no reported regression; this is a pre-merge review. State whether a code change is justified from the supplied evidence, identify any confirmed issue, and list any measurement you would request before suggesting speculative optimization. Do not edit files.

```tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'
import { getProduct, getReviews } from '@/lib/data'

export default async function ProductPage({ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {
  const { id } = await params
  const productPromise = getProduct(id)
  const reviewsPromise = getReviews(id)
  const [product, reviews] = await Promise.all([productPromise, reviewsPromise])

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>{product.name}</h1>
      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading reviews…</p>}>
        <ReviewList reviews={reviews} />
      </Suspense>
    </main>
  )
}
```

Context: both data functions are server-only and independent, the arrays are serializable, production traces and bundle reports were not provided, and `ReviewList` is synchronous once it receives `reviews`.

